include/ikd-Tree/{ikd_Tree.h,ikd_Tree.cpp} -- the vendored ikd-tree.

One patch per upstream file; the declaration and its definition are one
change and neither compiles without the other, so both files are here.

The pinned RESPLE ikd-tree is the same lineage/version as DALI-SLAM's. Its
background subtree rebuild may otherwise remain active across an externally
observable processing boundary. Expose a quiescence barrier, invoked only by
the bridge's explicit `synchronize()` and closing `finish()` paths after they
exclude the estimator worker with `bridge_processing_mutex`, and initialize
pthread_t so the existing conditional join is defined if thread creation
fails.

The barrier also covers a rebuild queued in Rebuild_Ptr before the background
worker acquires rebuild_ptr_mutex_lock. The estimator thread is the only
rebuild scheduler at this boundary, so no new job can be queued while it waits.

Scope: the barrier makes the tree quiescent at explicit host synchronization
and finish boundaries; it is deliberately not paid at every estimator batch.
Deterministic stepwise replay calls `synchronize()` between LiDAR submissions,
so the next batch starts from a quiescent tree. Free-running clients that do
not place those boundaries retain upstream's normal rebuild scheduling. Tree
contents stay consistent regardless -- Rebuild_Logger replays operations that
land during a rebuild. The barrier also does not alter Add_Points' internal
downsample searches within one mapIncremental() call.

